From: Jayanth Othayoth <ojayanth@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 07:03:35 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 07/12] event_extensions: add artifact storage support

Introduce generic artifact storage support for logging extensions.

The new utility allows plugins to persist binary payloads and
reference them through an ArtifactRef abstraction.

Keeping binary data outside descriptor and entry state reduces
memory usage and aligns with the transport-only handling of
extension metadata.

The implementation is intentionally generic so it can be reused
by future plugins requiring external artifact storage.

No functional changes are introduced by this commit.

Change-Id: I56c0ee27bece79e4dbdf8ad8bd050fad68ea00b0
Signed-off-by: Jayanth Othayoth <ojayanth@gmail.com>
